     The program first looks for a file named ".nethackrc" (without
the quotes) in your home directory, same as for Unix.  If that is
not found, it looks for "Library/Preferences/NetHack Defaults" below
your home directory.  And if that isn't found either, then it tries
again with the same name plus ".txt" appended.  Apparently the last
one is easier to edit for some folks since text editors recognize it
as containing plain text.


